<title>USA: Iomega Zip drive in new Macintosh series.</title>
<headline>Iomega Zip drive in new Macintosh series.</headline>
<dateline>ROY, Utah 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iomega Corp said Friday certain of Apple Computer's power Macintosh personal computers will use Iomega's internal Zip drive as a standard feature.</p>
<p>The company said the Zip drive to be in three of the new 6500 Macintosh series allows users to easily transfer large files and backup critical applications on Zip disks which provide 70 times the capacity of traditional floppy disks.</p>
<p>The company said it announced in February that it was shipping its Power Macintosh 8600, designed for Web developers, with an internal Zip drive as a standard feature.</p>
</text>
